WEBVTT

00:00.960 --> 00:10.980
MISSION: YOZAKURA FAMILY

00:11.147 --> 00:13.945
PLAN 27
MISSION COMPLETE / RECEPTION

00:14.278 --> 00:16.407
Kyoichiro!
He's going to blow up any second now!

00:16.407 --> 00:17.661
<i>I'm aware of that.</i>

00:17.661 --> 00:19.372
<i>We'll finish him off
with our next move.</i>

00:19.998 --> 00:21.000
Formation…

00:21.000 --> 00:22.629
Sakura Roots.

00:22.629 --> 00:23.506
Our axis…

00:23.923 --> 00:24.841
will be Taiyo!

00:25.133 --> 00:26.052
What?

00:26.637 --> 00:27.764
Taiyo?

00:28.181 --> 00:29.475
Wouldn't that be dangerous?

00:29.643 --> 00:31.437
Huh. Should be interesting!

00:31.605 --> 00:33.651
Not sure what you're going for, but…

00:34.443 --> 00:36.114
We're just going to have to do it.

00:42.711 --> 00:43.879
Let's go, Taiyo.

00:43.879 --> 00:44.756
Right.

00:46.384 --> 00:49.891
Man, can't believe they're making
the most ordinary of them lead the charge.

00:53.315 --> 00:54.693
Puppet Child.

00:57.657 --> 00:58.617
Ah…

00:59.410 --> 01:01.331
Super Taiyo…

01:01.540 --> 01:02.584
Festival!

01:02.584 --> 01:03.836
"SUPER TAIYO FESTIVAL"

01:04.378 --> 01:05.757
Melting Rock Glaive!

01:06.633 --> 01:07.468
Now, Big Sis!

01:07.927 --> 01:08.763
'Kay.

01:09.138 --> 01:10.140
There!

01:13.063 --> 01:14.440
You just don't learn, do you?

01:14.440 --> 01:17.488
What good would these rocks do now?

01:17.739 --> 01:19.951
<i>That's right, it's just a barrage.</i>

01:20.703 --> 01:22.414
<i>But one that happens to have…</i>

01:22.916 --> 01:25.253
<i>a slightly irregular stone in the mix.</i>

01:26.507 --> 01:28.385
<i>Enveloped in Shinzo's Turmeric,</i>

01:28.385 --> 01:30.180
<i>disguised as a rock by Kengo,</i>

01:30.180 --> 01:31.725
<i>guided by Shion's calculations,</i>

01:31.725 --> 01:35.525
<i>with Nanao's gas reinforcing his body
and the support of my threads,</i>

01:35.525 --> 01:37.737
<i>he's become a blade fired by Futaba…</i>

01:38.614 --> 01:41.077
<i>arriving unnoticed at his feet.</i>

01:44.125 --> 01:47.423
<i>An infiltration formation used to counter
underground explosives and bunkers…</i>

01:47.423 --> 01:48.676
<i>Sakura Roots.</i>

01:48.676 --> 01:50.847
<i>And Taiyo suggested it because…</i>

01:51.682 --> 01:52.767
<i>Big Bro Kyoichiro!</i>

01:54.938 --> 02:00.616
<i>…he was sure that something
was being stored under Kawashita's feet.</i>

02:07.964 --> 02:12.222
<i>This is the fourth mission,
shared only by you and me.</i>

02:13.057 --> 02:17.191
<i>We're going to recover my mother's body
without the other siblings catching on…</i>

02:18.026 --> 02:23.203
<i>and lay her to rest here,
on the Yozakura land where she was born.</i>

02:25.666 --> 02:28.589
With my enhanced eyes,
I can just barely see them.

02:29.298 --> 02:30.510
Shining threads!

02:33.306 --> 02:34.518
They must be…

02:38.609 --> 02:40.571
Correct.

02:40.821 --> 02:45.998
Red threads… crystallized someinine
woven by Yozakura blood.

02:46.499 --> 02:48.921
The Yozakura blood and heart,

02:48.921 --> 02:52.637
which never decompose even after death,
are too strong for humankind.

02:53.137 --> 02:57.312
But they can be used
as the foundation for spreading Hazakura.

02:57.856 --> 03:01.195
In order to protect Hazakura
and gain the power to spread it,

03:01.195 --> 03:05.078
I've had my body linked
to the body of the ninth head.

03:05.453 --> 03:09.128
Sever these,
and it will stop the flow of someinine

03:09.128 --> 03:12.426
and render me unable
to maintain my supply of Hazakura.

03:13.303 --> 03:14.764
It would destroy me.

03:14.764 --> 03:17.562
It's impossible for humans
to destroy this crystalized structure.

03:18.062 --> 03:20.943
Even if, by chance,
one thread were to be slashed,

03:20.943 --> 03:24.283
the someinine leaked from that severed end
would react with the air,

03:24.283 --> 03:26.120
and there'd be a huge explosion.

03:26.454 --> 03:30.755
Neither you nor the ninth head's corpse
would last two seconds.

03:48.456 --> 03:50.210
I know I don't stand a chance!

03:50.711 --> 03:51.546
But…

03:56.515 --> 03:59.521
…I can go beyond my limit
over and over!

04:00.438 --> 04:03.403
<i>I'm not going anywhere.</i>

04:04.238 --> 04:07.452
As long as you're always
by my side, Mutsumi!

04:09.164 --> 04:12.755
<i>I'll surpass it as many times as it takes!</i>

04:25.990 --> 04:27.200
Three times.

04:27.200 --> 04:28.871
Mission complete, eh?

04:29.622 --> 04:34.632
As a defensive power, Hardening is
ill-suited for simple attacks.

04:35.300 --> 04:36.427
However…

04:36.595 --> 04:39.642
that's precisely why,
in the case of this mission…

04:40.268 --> 04:45.236
it's the hardest blow ever,
that only Taiyo can unleash.

04:46.280 --> 04:47.784
There's been a change in Kawashita.

04:48.367 --> 04:50.539
His Hazakura levels are going down!

04:52.835 --> 04:55.508
<i>I can't maintain my body.</i>

04:55.508 --> 04:57.637
<i>I'm leaking Hazakura.</i>

04:58.346 --> 04:59.724
<i>No way out of it.</i>

04:59.724 --> 05:03.105
<i>I'll use my remaining strength to detonate
and release it into the ocean.</i>

05:03.565 --> 05:06.320
<i>Then my plan, while incomplete,
will be a success!</i>

05:07.405 --> 05:08.282
Oh, no!

05:12.290 --> 05:13.544
Storm Scabbard!

05:14.546 --> 05:16.883
I've sealed the energy from the explosion.

05:17.384 --> 05:21.100
Now you're going to pay
for what you did to our family,

05:21.100 --> 05:22.435
Makoto Kawashita.

05:23.814 --> 05:24.941
Purification!

05:25.776 --> 05:27.780
I've crystallized
the Hazakura in your body.

05:28.281 --> 05:30.034
Now you won't be able to blow it up!

05:31.412 --> 05:32.623
Synchro.

05:33.457 --> 05:37.132
<i>Decrease Kawashita's
someinine output to 10%.</i>

05:37.132 --> 05:38.301
Gotcha!

05:40.180 --> 05:41.223
"SERPENT WHEEL"

05:41.223 --> 05:42.602
Serpent Wheel!

05:45.649 --> 05:49.657
<i>Shrink him down to normal size
at a rate of one percent per second.</i>

05:49.657 --> 05:50.534
Roger that.

05:54.918 --> 05:55.753
Hollow Cocoon.

05:56.420 --> 05:59.343
I've sent countless microscopic threads
throughout your entire body,

05:59.343 --> 06:00.846
which are themselves harmless.

06:01.138 --> 06:04.562
That said, once they've permeated
every inch of your cells,

06:04.562 --> 06:06.858
they'll open you up
to all kinds of things.

06:12.077 --> 06:12.995
Accept it…

06:13.454 --> 06:15.208
the judgment that you have coming to you…

06:15.751 --> 06:17.337
with your whole body!

06:18.882 --> 06:20.134
Lightning Strike!

06:20.134 --> 06:21.345
"LIGHTNING STRIKE"

06:24.936 --> 06:28.860
<i>I'm being disassembled in my entirety.</i>

06:32.743 --> 06:33.954
<i>Mr. Kawashita?</i>

06:35.833 --> 06:38.797
<i>As it turns out,
your way didn't work, did it?</i>

06:39.423 --> 06:41.176
<i>You were too kind.</i>

06:42.387 --> 06:43.765
<i>I guess you're right.</i>

06:43.765 --> 06:45.561
<i>But I did get to enjoy myself immensely.</i>

06:46.061 --> 06:49.192
<i>Thanks for indulging me all this time.</i>

06:49.652 --> 06:52.700
<i>I'm the one who should be thanking you.</i>

06:53.492 --> 06:57.083
<i>I can now take the knowledge and results
from your long years of research</i>

06:57.083 --> 06:58.879
<i>and hand those over to him.</i>

06:59.547 --> 07:03.095
<i>The foundation that you built,
it will not have been for nothing.</i>

07:03.930 --> 07:05.099
<i>One hundred years.</i>

07:05.601 --> 07:07.730
<i>It was a brief but enjoyable time.</i>

07:08.230 --> 07:11.070
<i>Thank you… and…</i>

07:12.197 --> 07:15.537
goodbye, Mr. Kawashita.

07:26.391 --> 07:29.439
The Hazakura and someinine output…

07:29.732 --> 07:30.776
has been halted.

07:39.961 --> 07:41.631
Kyoichiro here.

07:41.631 --> 07:43.885
We've captured Kawashita.

07:43.885 --> 07:45.556
Everyone, report to me.

07:45.848 --> 07:49.020
Rin here. We've rescued the test subjects.

07:49.312 --> 07:53.237
Hotokeyama here.
We've subdued what's left of them.

07:55.993 --> 07:58.164
Thanks, Mutsumi.

07:59.207 --> 08:01.838
No, no, Taiyo.

08:01.838 --> 08:03.633
I should be…

08:04.009 --> 08:05.386
Good work!

08:09.060 --> 08:10.939
Mission: Yozakura Front Lines…

08:15.156 --> 08:16.450
is complete!

08:52.313 --> 08:54.777
What a beautiful cove, eh?

08:56.363 --> 08:57.490
Momo.

09:02.668 --> 09:05.089
Instead of saving Kawashita,
you stood by and watched

09:05.089 --> 09:07.343
and then left the island
as soon as he lost.

09:08.012 --> 09:09.932
You really are callous.

09:12.813 --> 09:14.441
You're not denying it?

09:14.441 --> 09:15.902
Well, why would you?

09:16.403 --> 09:19.660
From the start, you were never
going to do more than observe.

09:19.994 --> 09:22.165
The only thing that's important to you…

09:22.750 --> 09:24.377
is Rei's heart.

09:25.463 --> 09:28.260
She's my daughter.
Why don't you hand it over?

09:28.595 --> 09:30.348
I can't do that.

09:30.348 --> 09:33.020
Because it belongs to my wife and me.

09:33.813 --> 09:35.901
Well, you have a point.

09:37.571 --> 09:39.992
Guess I have no choice but to give up, eh?

09:40.744 --> 09:43.750
Like that would ever happen, right?
You scumbag son!

09:44.585 --> 09:45.837
Da Capo!

10:00.032 --> 10:03.205
Even my Winter Daphne can't absorb it all.

10:03.205 --> 10:04.332
Impressive.

10:05.292 --> 10:07.840
You gave me one last good memory.

10:09.426 --> 10:12.348
Goodbye, Father.

10:23.078 --> 10:24.665
Damn you.

10:27.754 --> 10:29.215
<i>Incident report…</i>

10:29.508 --> 10:33.683
<i>Makoto Kawashita, an executive
of the lawless organization, Tanpopo,</i>

10:33.683 --> 10:36.564
<i>was arrested in his research lab
on Skeleton Island.</i>

10:37.190 --> 10:38.985
<i>He stands accused
of weapons manufacturing,</i>

10:38.985 --> 10:41.031
<i>abduction and confinement,
human experimentation,</i>

10:41.031 --> 10:42.158
<i>and other numerous crimes.</i>

10:42.743 --> 10:46.500
<i>We will meet with the Spy Association,
the police, and other organizations</i>

10:46.500 --> 10:48.128
<i>to determine his sentence.</i>

10:48.378 --> 10:49.965
<i>The test subjects and armed henchmen,</i>

10:49.965 --> 10:52.220
<i>including the leaders
of the enemy faction Nijibana,</i>

10:52.220 --> 10:56.228
<i>will be placed under the surveillance
and protection of each organization</i>

10:56.228 --> 10:59.735
<i>after careful examination of their charges
and extenuating circumstances.</i>

11:00.069 --> 11:03.868
<i>A detailed report and invoice will follow.</i>

11:03.868 --> 11:05.246
<i>Please confirm receipt.</i>

11:07.543 --> 11:11.132
<i>The tenth head of the Yozakura family,
Mutsumi Yozakura.</i>

11:14.974 --> 11:17.521
Huh? It's this late already?

11:22.363 --> 11:24.325
I pulled an all-nighter.

11:43.698 --> 11:44.950
Nyaah!

11:45.367 --> 11:48.708
Sorry, Mutsumi.
I was onto you 100 meters out.

11:48.708 --> 11:49.918
That's my spy!

11:50.962 --> 11:52.758
Thanks for doing all this weeding.

11:52.758 --> 11:55.220
Sorry, I'm not sure
if the offering's right,

11:55.220 --> 11:56.849
since I only learned by example.

11:57.016 --> 11:58.853
You nailed it!

11:58.853 --> 12:01.817
Blue carnations
are my mother's and my flowers.

12:02.569 --> 12:04.782
Even if she's passed away,

12:05.157 --> 12:08.748
the head's blood never disappears,
and it resonates with me.

12:09.415 --> 12:12.463
I can tell that she's right here.

12:14.050 --> 12:17.766
Such an important mission, and you
were keeping it a secret from us.

12:18.935 --> 12:20.563
<i>As the eldest son, I kept it a sec--</i>

12:20.563 --> 12:21.941
<i>Shut up, you arrogant fool!</i>

12:22.441 --> 12:24.153
THE ELDEST SON BORE
THE BRUNT OF THE CENSURE
<i>The reaction was epic.</i>

12:24.905 --> 12:27.577
Retrieving your mother,
Kawashita, the test subjects,

12:27.577 --> 12:29.873
we succeeded in all that.

12:29.873 --> 12:32.587
But in the end, we couldn't find out
anything about your father.

12:33.422 --> 12:36.762
I promise you that I'll finish the job
one day, so wait for me, all right?

12:36.762 --> 12:39.017
Sure. First, though…

12:39.768 --> 12:44.026
ASANO FAMILY GRAVE
I should pay my respects
to your father, mother, and brother.

12:44.528 --> 12:45.487
Right.

12:48.661 --> 12:49.495
Taiyo?

12:51.667 --> 12:52.794
Thanks.

12:53.671 --> 12:54.506
Sure.

12:56.510 --> 13:01.019
<i>And so we all returned
from our spy mission</i>

13:01.019 --> 13:03.398
<i>back to our daily lives as a family.</i>

13:17.176 --> 13:18.596
Good morning…

13:19.138 --> 13:20.098
Taiyo.

13:24.900 --> 13:25.735
Huh?

13:26.904 --> 13:28.406
You're late, bridegroom!

13:29.117 --> 13:31.705
Huh?

13:31.705 --> 13:33.835
Come on,
let's get going.

13:33.835 --> 13:35.922
G-Go? Go where?

13:36.339 --> 13:39.345
To the Yozakura-style wedding reception,
what else?

13:39.847 --> 13:41.809
Wedding reception?

13:43.896 --> 13:45.567
Uh, thank you for coming

13:45.567 --> 13:51.286
to Mutsumi Yozakura and Taiyo Asano's
wedding reception today.

13:51.286 --> 13:54.458
Aside from those currently under arrest,
in exile, or deceased,

13:54.458 --> 13:58.676
we are truly grateful
to have you all here.

13:58.968 --> 14:01.849
We hope you enjoy yourselves 'til the end.

14:03.561 --> 14:04.813
What is this?

14:04.813 --> 14:07.569
Just what it looks like,
a wedding reception.

14:07.569 --> 14:09.113
For the industry, that is.

14:09.781 --> 14:14.040
Just like newly-appointed CEOs
make the rounds in normal companies,

14:14.040 --> 14:17.589
we hold this event to introduce
the new Yozakura head and her husband

14:17.589 --> 14:20.720
to those in the underworld
and everyone we do business with.

14:20.720 --> 14:25.270
Well, some of them are clearly
not here for the introduction part.

14:25.270 --> 14:26.565
Oh, it's all right.

14:27.066 --> 14:30.823
You know how so many people in this
industry have all kinds of baggage.

14:30.823 --> 14:34.873
So this is one day that everyone
can forget which side they're on

14:34.873 --> 14:36.292
and just let loose.

14:36.585 --> 14:39.090
If you don't want to get pinched now,

14:39.090 --> 14:43.098
give up everything you know
about the boss of that black-market route.

14:43.098 --> 14:44.893
Otherwise, I'm tossing your butts in jail.

14:44.893 --> 14:47.732
Hey, come on, man. Give us a break.

14:47.941 --> 14:50.487
They're letting loose in a disturbing way.

14:51.615 --> 14:53.995
But, hey, sorry I surprised you like that.

14:53.995 --> 14:56.583
They suddenly decided
this morning to do this.

14:56.583 --> 14:58.086
Th-This morning?

14:58.336 --> 15:00.508
A scammer who just
broke out of prison yesterday,

15:00.508 --> 15:02.595
a back-alley doctor
who has to operate tomorrow,

15:02.595 --> 15:05.142
an artist spy
in the middle of a world tour…

15:05.643 --> 15:08.566
It's really hard to schedule things
when you work in the underworld.

15:08.691 --> 15:10.778
I-I see.

15:11.237 --> 15:15.037
Also, since we just finished
the mission on Skeleton Island,

15:15.037 --> 15:16.707
the timing seemed to be right.

15:17.876 --> 15:19.671
Bridegroom Mr. Taiyo?

15:20.088 --> 15:24.388
The oldest currently active spy,
Mr. Fuma, would like to say hello to you.

15:25.683 --> 15:26.935
U-Uh…

15:27.896 --> 15:29.106
Th-Thank you very--

15:36.370 --> 15:39.126
Dodging my wedding gift…

15:39.836 --> 15:41.590
Not half bad!

15:41.799 --> 15:43.552
Grandpa! Grandma!

15:43.761 --> 15:46.474
So sorry.
He just couldn't contain his excitement.

15:46.474 --> 15:48.854
How long has it been
since we last disguised ourselves?

15:48.854 --> 15:50.775
Well, it's a reception,
so I couldn't resist.

15:50.775 --> 15:52.444
We must congratulate our grandchildren

15:52.444 --> 15:54.365
with plenty of murderous intent,
after all!

15:54.365 --> 15:56.537
<i>Scary! What do you mean? Scary!</i>

15:56.537 --> 15:59.333
In the underworld, a reception is
for celebrating, but also a venue

15:59.333 --> 16:01.672
to determine whether you're
worthy to be celebrated or not.

16:02.214 --> 16:06.347
As someone you'll be sharing risks with
as a colleague, it won't do to be weak.

16:06.347 --> 16:08.686
And that goes for the family, too.

16:09.061 --> 16:14.196
A venue for testing just how trustworthy
the new head's system is…

16:14.446 --> 16:16.827
at Yozakura-style wedding receptions,
that's tradition!

16:17.202 --> 16:18.163
A fish?

16:18.454 --> 16:21.795
This is the Congratulatory Suit worn
by the eldest child on joyous occasions.

16:21.795 --> 16:22.672
It's a tradition.

16:23.214 --> 16:26.387
What a drastic turnaround
from the other day's serious mission!

16:28.224 --> 16:30.020
In other words, at this reception,

16:30.020 --> 16:32.107
you and Mutsumi's lives
will be on the line

16:32.107 --> 16:35.363
as they test you to see
whether you're worthy as work allies.

16:35.781 --> 16:39.038
Make sure this reception
doesn't turn into a funeral!

16:39.038 --> 16:43.505
If only you'd finished off Momo
at Rei's reception…

16:43.714 --> 16:46.678
Then we wouldn't be
in this complicated mess now.

16:47.597 --> 16:49.976
Hey, not funny! Not funny at all!

16:50.101 --> 16:51.939
Anyway, that's the story.

16:52.397 --> 16:55.070
But it's not like I want you to die,

16:55.070 --> 16:56.990
and I'm not wearing this black tie--

16:56.990 --> 16:59.871
which you don't at receptions
because they call to mind funerals--

16:59.871 --> 17:02.417
just to rub it in your face, all right?

17:02.669 --> 17:05.382
<i>Oh, man, it's been a while
since he's been like this.</i>

17:05.967 --> 17:07.929
I'll be the one
to guard Mutsumi with my life.

17:07.929 --> 17:10.601
Meaning that
the biggest sucker here today…

17:10.601 --> 17:11.435
Huh?

17:11.435 --> 17:12.897
…is you, Taiyo.

17:12.897 --> 17:14.567
I'd have to agree!

17:14.776 --> 17:17.489
Now, then, everyone.
He's got a bounty on his head,

17:17.489 --> 17:19.828
so what a perfect wedding favor,
am I right?

17:19.828 --> 17:21.497
Eldest son, you bastard!

17:22.416 --> 17:25.673
<i>Look here, Kyoichiro.
That's enough of that.</i>

17:26.090 --> 17:27.217
<i>Mutsumi?</i>

17:27.217 --> 17:28.386
<i>No, it's not her.</i>

17:30.015 --> 17:31.058
<i>Is this…</i>

17:31.977 --> 17:33.062
Mo…

17:33.354 --> 17:34.774
Mom!

17:36.027 --> 17:37.404
<i>Mama…</i>

17:37.905 --> 17:41.663
<i>What are you recording this for, Mom?
I'm not doing anything.</i>

17:42.164 --> 17:44.878
<i>It's a video letter
for Mutsumi's wedding reception.</i>

17:45.378 --> 17:49.763
<i>I just know that you'll be up to no good,
so I scolded you in advance.</i>

17:50.013 --> 17:51.933
That's Mutsumi when she was two.

17:51.933 --> 17:54.229
So that makes me seven, huh?

17:54.480 --> 17:57.152
I can't believe she left behind
a video letter like this.

17:58.196 --> 18:00.200
<i>What are you talking about, Mom?</i>

18:00.200 --> 18:05.210
<i>I adore Mutsumi so much. I'd never
stir up any trouble at her celebration.</i>

18:05.210 --> 18:06.588
<i>Big Bro, no!</i>

18:07.381 --> 18:11.138
<i>I'm worried
because you adore her so much.</i>

18:13.602 --> 18:16.775
Futaba! I wasn't aware
that this video existed!

18:16.775 --> 18:18.069
Of course not.

18:18.361 --> 18:23.496
Mom gave it to me for safekeeping
years ago to admonish you.

18:23.496 --> 18:26.795
<i>There, there. You're safe now, Mutsumi.</i>

18:26.795 --> 18:27.672
<i>Big Sis!</i>

18:27.672 --> 18:30.009
You sure haven't changed at all,
Big Sis Futaba!

18:30.009 --> 18:31.220
You're like a phantom.

18:31.220 --> 18:35.604
<i>Let me go! Give me back my Mutsumi!</i>

18:35.604 --> 18:38.109
And Big Bro hasn't changed a bit, either.

18:38.109 --> 18:39.319
He's a pervert.

18:39.319 --> 18:40.363
<i>Come on, now.</i>

18:40.363 --> 18:43.077
<i>Children, don't fight.</i>

18:43.579 --> 18:45.248
Mother.

18:58.525 --> 19:00.111
Mom.

19:05.623 --> 19:08.127
<i>I'm seven, so I'm really strong, you know!</i>

19:08.127 --> 19:10.633
<i>I'm the eldest son! Now hand over Mutsumi!</i>

19:10.758 --> 19:12.678
<i>We started going on missions
at the same age.</i>

19:12.678 --> 19:14.348
<i>Let's see you take her back if you can!</i>

19:18.356 --> 19:20.736
<i>Congratulations on getting married,
Mutsumi.</i>

19:20.736 --> 19:24.786
<i>I'm sure that it's way more
of a hot mess over there than it is here.</i>

19:25.495 --> 19:30.756
<i>You never know, that Kyoichiro
might even try to kill your husband.</i>

19:30.756 --> 19:32.467
<i>Mother sure knows best!</i>

19:32.843 --> 19:36.183
<i>The other day, your father
came this close to dying, you see.</i>

19:36.183 --> 19:38.939
<i>And that made me think
that I might not have much longer myself,</i>

19:38.939 --> 19:41.443
<i>so I decided to record this video
in a hurry.</i>

19:41.903 --> 19:44.701
<i>She's saying these terrifying things
without batting an eyelash.</i>

19:44.701 --> 19:46.913
<i>And the facts are way too heavy.</i>

19:46.913 --> 19:50.378
<i>I have no clue
what the right way to respond would be.</i>

19:50.629 --> 19:54.887
<i>I'm sorry for bringing you all
into such a chaotic family.</i>

19:54.887 --> 19:58.937
<i>But you know what? It gave me great joy
to spend time with you.</i>

19:59.898 --> 20:03.070
<i>I want you to have a family
that will make you feel that way, too.</i>

20:03.614 --> 20:05.993
<i>That's what I wish for you.</i>

20:07.203 --> 20:08.497
Mom.

20:08.832 --> 20:11.086
<i>And now, Mutsumi's husband.</i>

20:11.963 --> 20:14.134
<i>Thank you for choosing Mutsumi.</i>

20:14.636 --> 20:18.644
<i>Supporting her in her destiny
will be extremely difficult…</i>

20:19.436 --> 20:22.317
<i>but I'm counting on you
to look after my daughter.</i>

20:28.496 --> 20:29.331
Right!

20:35.426 --> 20:37.556
Acting like her husband!

20:37.556 --> 20:40.103
Well, he is her husband, Big Bro.

20:40.103 --> 20:41.188
Big Sis Mutsumi!

20:41.188 --> 20:43.317
I think we've reached the time limit!

20:45.071 --> 20:46.031
All right, then.

20:48.327 --> 20:53.254
So, everyone, thank you for coming today.
We're truly grateful to you.

20:53.755 --> 20:56.803
As the tenth head of the Yozakura family,

20:56.803 --> 20:59.349
I will do all that I can
to protect the Yozakura spy family

20:59.349 --> 21:04.067
left to me by my predecessor, my mother.

21:04.317 --> 21:06.865
So please continue to support me.

21:15.339 --> 21:17.803
And now, ladies and gentlemen,
please stand up.

21:17.803 --> 21:19.974
As we embark
on a new chapter of our lives,

21:19.974 --> 21:23.648
please see us off
in a thunderous barrage of bullets.

21:26.153 --> 21:27.865
What?

21:28.240 --> 21:30.579
At the end, the bride and groom
walk down the aisle

21:30.579 --> 21:32.290
in a hail of baptismal bullets.

21:32.290 --> 21:34.796
That's another Yozakura-style
wedding reception tradition!

21:35.087 --> 21:37.760
I object to your traditions!

21:38.427 --> 21:39.639
Don't worry.

21:40.516 --> 21:42.686
Everyone will be protecting us.

21:42.686 --> 21:44.147
Come on, let's go!

21:45.149 --> 21:47.655
I'm still counting on you, Taiyo.

21:51.370 --> 21:52.205
Right!

22:12.203 --> 22:15.459
<i>For Mutsumi, me…</i>

22:16.671 --> 22:17.923
<i> and the Yozakura spy family…</i>

22:21.054 --> 22:22.683
<i>this was our new chapter.</i>

22:25.981 --> 22:27.985
MISSION: YOZAKURA FAMILY

23:32.322 --> 23:33.240
KILL
